From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: IamMaxim <g.maxim.stepanoff@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 28 May 2026 19:49:46 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] strip: remove telemetry crate and call sites

Removes the telemetry crate, all telemetry::event!(...) invocations
(188 across 32 crates), use telemetry::* imports, and the
'telemetry.workspace = true' Cargo deps. telemetry_events crate is
kept; its remaining consumers (client/collab/zed_llm_client/edit_prediction)
are stripped in subsequent patches.

Build-fixup details:
  - client/src/telemetry.rs:248 ::telemetry::init(tx) -> drop(tx).
    The local mpsc channel had its sender registered with the now-deleted
    telemetry crate's global; dropping it instead lets the consumer loop
    terminate immediately.
  - client/src/client.rs: re-add 'use crate::telemetry::Telemetry;'. The
    upstream 'use telemetry::Telemetry;' line was a same-name path collision
    that actually resolved to the local module, not the extern crate.
  - agent_ui/src/conversation_view.rs:1788,1832: '=> ,' empty match arms
    fixed to '=> {},' (strip script left these as residue).
  - zed/src/reliability.rs:320: orphan '::' fragment removed (strip script
    left this as residue from '::telemetry::event!').

Warnings remain (unused variables in let-bindings whose only consumer was
the stripped event! call). They are cosmetic and will largely disappear
when client, crashes, and the agent code paths are stripped in later patches.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
